          "content": {
            "id": "08f6bb65-9347-3f10-a0ae-c4e2df6361bd",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Cava stock falls after lowering sales growth forecast",
            "description": "<p>Cava (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/CAVA\">CAVA</a>) reported third quarter adjusted earnings per share of $0.12, which was short of the Bloomberg consensus estimate of $0.13. Revenue was higher than Wall Street expected. Comparable same-restaurant sales growth fell short of expectations, 1.9% versus an estimated 2.67%. The company also lowered its full-year comparable sales growth forecast to a range of 3% to 4%. It had been 4% to 6%.</p>\n<p>Yahoo Finance Senior Reporter <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/brooke-dipalma/\">Brooke DiPalma</a> recaps the results.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/asking-for-a-trend/\">Asking for a Trend</a>.</p>",
            "summary": "Cava (CAVA) reported third quarter adjusted earnings per share of $0.12, which was short of the Bloomberg consensus estimate of $0.13. Revenue was higher than Wall Street expected. Comparable same-restaurant sales growth fell short of expectations, 1.9% versus an estimated 2.67%. The company also lowered its full-year comparable sales growth forecast to a range of 3% to 4%. It had been 4% to 6%. Yahoo Finance Senior Reporter Brooke DiPalma recaps the results. To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more Asking for a Trend.",
